    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d809">

                <pb facs="0866" n="856" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg856"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690.419/6–2149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-21T15:00:00+01:00">June 21, 1949—3 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 21—10:09 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2390. For Gay,<anchor n="43" xml:id="d809-f1"/> CP, and Bell,<anchor n="44"
                        xml:id="d809-f2"/> OIT, from Martin and McIntyre. First session with British
                    today resulted satisfactory exploration problems involved application export
                    controls China.</p>
                <p>Session tomorrow considering detailof commodity and country coverage. We require
                    soonest Washington suggestions selected list key 1B items essential for prompt
                    UK control.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d809-f1" n="43" xml:id="d809-f1-content">
                <p>Merrill C. Gay, Assistant Chief of the Division of Commercial Policy.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d809-f2" n="44" xml:id="d809-f2-content">
                <p>George L. Bell, Associate Director of the Office of International Trade,
                    Department of Commerce.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
